  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resilient Women, Resilient Communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">-Strengthen women&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;s economic empowerment and household resilience

-Improve children&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;s access to food, education and health through stable livelihoods

-Increase climate adaptation in small-scale livelihood activities

-Build sustainable organisational capacity of a local NGO to operate independently and attract diversified funding</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project strengthens economic resilience among vulnerable women-led households in Eastern Uganda through climate-adapted livelihoods, while simultaneously building long-term organisational capacity of a local civil society organisation. The intervention combines direct household-level livelihood support, community-based learning and dissemination, and structured organisational development focused on results management, reporting, fundraising and accountability.</narrative>
  </description>
